H200.definition:
from the same as H191 (אֱוִיל);
silliness
KJV: folly, foolishly(-ness).

H201.definition:
from H559 (אָמַר); talkative;
Omar, a grandson of Esau
KJV: Omar.

H202.definition:
probably from the same as H205 (אָוֶן) (in the sense of effort, but successful);
ability, power, (figuratively) wealth
KJV: force, goods, might, strength, substance.

H203.definition:
