Aven, the contemptuous synonym of three places, one in Coele-Syria, one in Egypt (On), and one in Palestine (Bethel)
KJV: Aven. See also H204 (אוֹן), H1007 (בֵּית אָוֶן).

H207.definition:
or (shortened) אֹנוֹ; prolonged from H202 (אוֹן); strong;
Ono, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ono.

H208.definition:
a variation of H209 (אוֹנָן); strong;
Onam, the name of an Edomite and of an Israelite
KJV: Onam.

H209.definition:
a variation of H207 (אוֹנוֹ); strong;
Onan, a son of Judah
KJV: Onan.

H210.definition:
perhaps a corruption of H211 (אוֹפִיר);
Uphaz, a famous gold region
KJV: Uphaz.

H211.definition:
or (shortened) אֹפִיר; and אוֹפִר; of uncertain derivation;
Ophir, the name of a son of Joktan, and of a gold region in the East
KJV: Ophir.

H212.definition:
or (shortened) אֹפָן; from an unused root meaning to revolve;
a wheel
KJV: wheel.

H213.definition:
a primitive root;
to press; (by implication) to be close, hurry, withdraw
KJV: (make) haste(-n, -y), labor, be narrow.

H214.definition:
from H686 (אָצַר);
a depository
KJV: armory, cellar, garner, store(-house), treasure(-house) (-y).

H215.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causative, make) luminous (literally and metaphorically)
KJV: [idiom] break of day, glorious, kindle, (be, en-, give, show) light (-en, -ened), set on fire, shine.

H216.definition:
from H215 (אוֹר);
illumination or (concrete) luminary (in every sense, including lightning, happiness, etc.)
KJV: bright, clear, [phrase] day, light (-ning), morning, sun.

H217.definition:
